Foundation → Steam Recipe Matrix

Purpose

This document defines the first concrete recipe layer of the pack.

The Foundation phase preserves vanilla survival while preparing the player for industrial progression.

The Primitive Age introduces the first processed industrial materials.

The Steam Age introduces the first real industrial infrastructure.

Rules

Vanilla survival remains accessible at the start.

Modded machines must not provide an immediate alternative to the main progression.

Primitive components must establish the materials needed for Steam.

Steam machines must require infrastructure built during the Primitive Age.

Recipes should create dependencies between materials, machines, power, and automation.

No recipe should require large quantities only to simulate difficulty.

Foundation

Vanilla crafting remains available for basic survival equipment.

Vanilla progression reaches Netherite normally.

Modded technological machines, generators, advanced storage, digital logistics, and high-tier processing are gated.

Primitive Age

Primitive progression begins after the vanilla foundation.

Primitive components should use processed iron, copper, basic steel preparation, and other low-tier materials available before electrical technology.

Primitive recipes should favor manual and semi-automated processing.

The purpose of the Primitive Age is to make the limitations of manual processing visible and create the need for Steam.

Steam Age

Steam is the first major industrial power system.

Steam machines should require Primitive components and infrastructure.

Create mechanical systems become useful for material handling, mechanical processing, transportation, and early automation.

GregTech remains the primary technological progression.

Modern Industrialization supplements the progression without creating a parallel route around GregTech.

First Cross-Mod Dependencies

Early industrial components may combine:

GregTech processed materials

Modern Industrialization machine components

Create mechanical components

Basic infrastructure from vanilla

These dependencies must be introduced gradually.

Progression Integrity

A recipe is progression-breaking if it allows access to a later technological tier without completing the required previous infrastructure.

Any such recipe must be removed or replaced through KubeJS.

Implementation

This matrix is the foundation for the first KubeJS recipe implementation.

The next implementation pass should convert these rules into concrete item and machine recipes, beginning with Primitive components and the first Steam machines.

All recipes must be tested in-game before the next progression layer is added.
